-- 1. The Plaza Hotel
('11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000001',
'The Plaza Hotel',
'Midtown',
'Hotel Lobby',
'There is no more loaded address in New York than the southeast corner of Central Park. Eloise lived here. Cary Grant fled assassins here. The lobby is a gilded holding pen for the quietly famous, the obviously rich, and the people who want to feel what that feels like for the price of an afternoon tea. Sit in the Palm Court, order something in a flute, and hold it as though you are accustomed to holding things in flutes.',
40.7646310, -73.9743240,
NULL,
4,
'{"men": {"brands": ["Brioni", "Kiton", "Patek Philippe", "John Lobb"], "outfit": {"top": "Pale grey or cream sport coat, white shirt open at the collar", "bottom": "Charcoal flannel trousers with a clean break", "shoes": "Black or chestnut cap-toe Oxfords, highly polished", "bag": "Slim leather document holder or nothing at all", "accessories": "Patek Philippe or vintage Rolex, no other jewelry, pocket square in ivory linen"}, "color_palette": "Charcoal, cream, ivory — the palette of a man who once owned a racehorse without mentioning it", "budget_dupe": "A well-pressed suit from J.Crew or SuitSupply in grey, resoled leather shoes. The Plaza lobby is dark enough for ambition to pass as breeding."}, "women": {"brands": ["Oscar de la Renta", "The Row", "Cartier", "Manolo Blahnik"], "outfit": {"top": "Structured blazer in ivory or pale blush, or a silk blouse in cream with pearl buttons", "bottom": "Tailored wide-leg trousers in champagne or cream", "shoes": "Pointed-toe kitten heel in nude or black", "bag": "Structured top-handle in black or tan, no visible logos", "accessories": "Cartier Love bracelet, pearl drop earrings, single delicate gold chain"}, "color_palette": "Ivory, champagne, nude, blush — afternoon tea at the most famous hotel in America", "budget_dupe": "Banana Republic blazer in cream, well-cut trousers from COS, one serious secondhand bag from a consignment shop. You are doing afternoon tea, not the Met Gala."}}',
true),

-- 2. The St. Regis New York
('11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000001',
'The St. Regis New York',
'Midtown',
'Continental',
'John Jacob Astor IV built this hotel in 1904 and it has never fully recovered from having good taste. The King Cole Bar — with its Maxfield Parrish mural of Old King Cole — is one of the few places in Manhattan where you can order a Bloody Mary with the sincere belief that it was invented here. The butler service still exists. The room still matters. Order something red, look at the mural, and try to look unsurprised.',
40.7613000, -73.9744530,
NULL,
4,
'{"men": {"brands": ["Tom Ford", "Huntsman", "A. Lange & Söhne", "Crockett & Jones"], "outfit": {"top": "Midnight navy suit with a faint chalk stripe, or a charcoal blazer with white shirt", "bottom": "Matching trousers, full break, nothing modern", "shoes": "Black cap-toe Oxfords or dark burgundy loafers with tassels", "bag": "Nothing. Possibly an overcoat over one arm.", "accessories": "A. Lange & Söhne or Jaeger-LeCoultre, silk pocket square in ivory or pale gold"}, "color_palette": "Midnight navy, charcoal, ivory — the palette of someone who considers a Bloody Mary a medical prescription", "budget_dupe": "A good suit from SuitSupply in navy or charcoal. The King Cole Bar is lit for maximum atmosphere and minimum scrutiny. Fit matters more than label."}, "women": {"brands": ["Valentino", "Carolina Herrera", "Van Cleef & Arpels", "Roger Vivier"], "outfit": {"top": "Silk blouse in dusty rose or champagne, or a shift dress in pale gold", "bottom": "Straight-leg cigarette trousers or an A-line midi skirt in deep ivory", "shoes": "Block-heel court shoe in black or nude, or an embellished flat for afternoon", "bag": "Small structured top-handle or a beaded evening clutch if after 7pm", "accessories": "Van Cleef Alhambra or a serious vintage brooch, pearl earrings, a single thin bracelet"}, "color_palette": "Dusty rose, champagne, pale gold — someone who found this hotel in a novel and has never fully left", "budget_dupe": "A good silk blouse from Equipment or a vintage find, clean trousers from & Other Stories. The Maxfield Parrish mural is the most valuable thing in the room — stand near it."}}',
true),

-- 3. The Carlyle Hotel
('11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000001',
'The Carlyle Hotel',
'Upper East Side',
'Old Money',
'The Carlyle is not a hotel in the ordinary sense. It is a residential building that tolerates guests. World leaders have stayed here. JFK had a permanent suite. The Café Carlyle runs one of the last great cabaret programs in America. Even if you''re only walking through the lobby, you will feel a quality of hush that only comes from decades of important people having private conversations in upholstered chairs.',
40.7743370, -73.9631320,
NULL,
5,
'{"men": {"brands": ["Brioni", "Huntsman Savile Row", "Patek Philippe", "Lobb"], "outfit": {"top": "Dark navy double-breasted blazer or a charcoal suit — this is a proper dress code building", "bottom": "Matching or coordinated trousers, perfectly pressed", "shoes": "Black cap-toes or dark Oxford, mirror shine", "bag": "Nothing or a slim leather attaché", "accessories": "Patek Philippe Calatrava in yellow gold, silk pocket square in deep burgundy, nothing else"}, "color_palette": "Dark navy, charcoal, black, ivory — the palette of a man who has attended events he cannot discuss", "budget_dupe": "SuitSupply Napoli in charcoal. You are walking through one of the most serious lobbies in New York. Buy one good suit and mean it."}, "women": {"brands": ["The Row", "Bottega Veneta", "Cartier", "Manolo Blahnik"], "outfit": {"top": "Long-sleeve silk dress in midnight blue or deep emerald, or a cashmere blazer over wide-leg trousers", "bottom": "Tailored wide-leg trousers in charcoal or a structured midi skirt", "shoes": "Classic pointed-toe heel in black or navy, no platforms", "bag": "Bottega Veneta Jodie or a small structured Kelly-style bag — no visible branding", "accessories": "Cartier Trinity ring or thin gold chain, small diamond studs, possibly gloves in cool weather"}, "color_palette": "Midnight blue, deep emerald, charcoal — someone whose composure is structural, not performed", "budget_dupe": "A well-cut dress from Theory or Vince in a dark solid colour. The Carlyle rewards restraint at every price point."}}',
true),

-- 4. Baccarat Hotel & Residences
('11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000001',
'Baccarat Hotel New York',
'Midtown',
'Hotel Lobby',
'The most crystalline hotel in the city — 4,500 pieces of Baccarat crystal deployed without a hint of apology. The lobby bar is genuinely one of the most beautiful rooms in Midtown, which is a low bar until you see it and revise your opinion upward. The Grand Salon has the quality of light that makes everyone look slightly more important than they are. Use it accordingly.',
