-- 6. The Beekman Hotel
('11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000001',
'The Beekman Hotel',
'Financial District',
'Hotel Lobby',
'A restored 1883 neo-Gothic tower in the Financial District with a nine-story atrium that is one of the most architecturally significant interiors in New York. The atrium lobby looks like someone took a Victorian birdcage and filled it with good taste. Tom Colicchio''s restaurant occupies the ground floor. The crowd is media, finance, and the occasional academic who can''t believe this exists downtown.',
