-- 12. Edge at Hudson Yards
('11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000001',
'Edge at Hudson Yards',
'Hudson Yards',
'Art World',
'The highest outdoor sky deck in the Western Hemisphere, which is a fact that stops feeling abstract when you are standing on a glass-floored triangle projecting 100 stories over the Hudson River. The views take in the entirety of lower and midtown Manhattan, the Hudson, and on clear days, New Jersey in a way that almost makes New Jersey look acceptable. The champagne bar up here is a reasonable idea that the altitude makes feel inevitable.',
40.7537000, -74.0023000,
NULL,
2,
'{"men": {"brands": ["Practical and photogenic"], "outfit": {"top": "Clean solid-colour sweatshirt or structured shirt — wind is a factor at 100 floors", "bottom": "Dark jeans or trousers — it can be cold even in summer", "shoes": "Clean sneakers or loafers with grip", "bag": "Small backpack or nothing", "accessories": "Sunglasses — essential — and a watch that photographs well against the skyline"}, "color_palette": "Navy, black, slate — colours that work against sky. Avoid white in direct sun at this altitude.", "budget_dupe": "Any clean, fitted outfit in a solid colour. The Hudson Yards architecture has strong opinions and your outfit is a footnote."}, "women": {"brands": ["Practical chic"], "outfit": {"top": "A fitted turtleneck or structured jacket — the deck is exposed and the wind is real", "bottom": "Tailored trousers or straight-leg jeans", "shoes": "Sneakers or block-heel boots with grip — glass floor, some movement", "bag": "Crossbody with a zip — the wind has opinions about open bags at this altitude", "accessories": "Secure earrings, no scarves unless tied tightly, sunglasses are essential"}, "color_palette": "Jewel tones work beautifully at altitude — cobalt, emerald, deep burgundy against the sky and river", "budget_dupe": "The observation deck itself is the experience. Dress for wind and glass floors and you''ve made the correct choice."}}',
